<pre class=metadata>
Title: Keyboard Media Queries
Shortname: keyboard-media-queries
Level: none
Status: LD
ED: https://arronei.github.io/CSS-Additions/system-media-queries/keyboard/spec/
Repository: arronei/CSS-Additions
Editor: Arron Eicholz
Abstract: This specification adds two media features about keyboards. '@media/keyboard' reports whether
    a hardware keyboard is available, so pages can show keyboard shortcuts only to people who can use them,
    which '@media/pointer' and '@media/hover' can't tell. '@media/virtual-keyboard' reports whether an
    on-screen keyboard is covering part of the page, so pages can hide toolbars and footers that would
    otherwise sit on top of it. Neither reveals the keyboard's layout, language, or size. Keyboards used by
    assistive technology don't count, embedded content learns only about its own input, and attaching a
    keyboard can't be used to link visits to different sites.
Markup Shorthands: markdown yes, css yes
Complain About: accidental-2119 no, missing-example-ids yes
Assume Explicit For: yes
</pre>

